103:/*
104:DESCRIPTION
105:This PAL contains the logic to back drive the 386 byte enables during the non 
106:CPU operations. It decodes the address inputs and drives the appropriate BEx 
107:lines whenever the 386 is in a HLDA state.

LISTING FOR LOGIC DESCRIPTION FILE: D4-SADI.pld                      Page 3

CUPL(WM): Universal Compiler for Programmable Logic
